{
  "configuration_id": "config_047",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_004: multimodal/multiprofile/pca_n2000/resnet50/avgpool/concat → 61.9% acc, 36.42 GPU hrs), evidence is sparse and the priority is to identify the highest-leverage design axis. The image encoder is the most likely single source of large improvement: ResNet50 (~25M params) is substantially smaller and less expressive than an ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L (~300M+ params), so upgrading it should yield a meaningful accuracy gain if the image modality is informative. config_047 changes only the image encoder (resnet50 → imagenet_vit_l) while holding RNA encoder (pca_n2000), aggregation (avgpool), and fusion (concat) identical to the baseline, giving a clean single-variable comparison. This is the best use of experiment 2 because it reduces the largest uncertainty (whether a stronger image representation helps) before committing budget to more expensive combinations (e.g., transformer aggregation + ViT-L + scgpt). Expected relative cost: roughly 1.5–2× the baseline (~50–70 GPU hrs) due to the larger ViT-L backbone, which is justified by the expected accuracy gain and the information gained for all subsequent ViT-L-based experiments."
}

